// @check
// @error-at 27:8 flows into `printString` expecting string
// @error-at 31:13 flows into `printString` expecting string
// SOUNDNESS REGRESSION NET for the deferred join (see
// `hole-is-guard-return-join-reject.vl`). A join that this checker no longer
// collapses eagerly must not lose the rejection the collapse used to provide.
//
// `pick`'s returns join two hole params. Reaching a CONCRETE parameter from inside
// ANOTHER generic body, the collapse produced a hole-typed argument, so
// `noteArgCstr` recorded the demand and the outer call re-validated it. The first
// cut of the deferred join dropped the hole arm instead, reported plain `string`,
// recorded NOTHING, and emitted invalid wasm ("expected (ref $type), found i32")
// for a spelling that used to be caught cleanly.
//
// Two rules keep this rejecting: an arm that merely resolved to ANOTHER hole is
// undecided, never "provably dead" (only a derived read off a CONCRETE pin can be
// proven unreachable), and a join the re-fold cannot decide COLLAPSES rather than
// escaping as a placeholder union. `inference/hole-join-generic-arg.vl` is the
// must-not-error twin.
function pick(a, b, c) {
  if c then return a
  return b
}
function printString(thing: string) { print(thing) }

// One hole arm, one concrete arm. The i32 pin cannot reach a `string` parameter.
function goOne(x) { printString(pick(x, "s", true)) }
goOne(1)

// BOTH arms holes — decided only when the outer call pins them, and they disagree.
function goTwo(x, y) { printString(pick(x, y, true)) }
goTwo(1, "s")
